Run:

Shell
curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"

Verify:

Shell
ls -l kubectl

You should see something like:

Plain Text
-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 60M kubectl
Make executable
Shell
chmod +x kubectl
Move to system path
Shell
sudo mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/
Verify installation
Shell
kubectl version --client

Expected:

Plain Text
Client Version: v1.xx.x
 
Alternative (Ubuntu apt package)

If the download method is failing:

Shell
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y kubernetes-client

Verify:

Shell
kubectl version --client
Check PATH

After installation:

Shell
which kubectl

Expected:

Plain Text
/usr/local/bin/kubectl

If you're installing Minikube + kubectl + Helm + ArgoCD on your Ubuntu VM, run:

Shell
which kubectl
which minikube
which helm

and share the output. That will confirm which components are installed and which still need to be configured.
